    {
      "version": "6.1",
      "releaseNotes": "- The most anticipated feature is finally here: you can now drag pieces to edit and analyze moves in any position\n- The engine will now analyze and display the top moves in a position\n- A new banner in the game screen will let you know when a new move has happened while not at the most up-to-date position\n- Several engine optimizations",
      "seenAt": "2021-05-27T19:54:15Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "6.2",
      "releaseNotes": "- Added ability to search for tournaments\n- Added ability to filter games\n- Engine settings allows you to change engine depth\n- Added ability to reload tournaments\n- Games will no longer be out of date when coming back from the background\n- Engine optimizations\n- Translated app into several languages, with more to come!",
      "seenAt": "2021-06-26T20:58:47Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "6.3",
      "releaseNotes": "- Engine analysis will now display additional context for the best moves.\n- Added more data to standings, like player performance and ELO change.\n- Optimized energy consumption of the different engine depth settings.\n- Several improvements for the upcoming FIDE World Cup.\n",
      "seenAt": "2021-07-10T13:28:21Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "7.0",
      "releaseNotes": "This app has been updated by Apple to prepare for watchOS 27 compatibility. No new features are included.\n\n- New Game Report allows you to analyze games using the new Game Report to find the critical moves.\n- Optimized for the upcoming version of iOS.\n",
      "seenAt": "2021-09-17T23:03:34Z"
    },
